On 7/13/06, Chris Capel <pdf23ds@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> If English *did* have Lojban-style phrase terminators, how often would
> they be required? Less than Lojban, because English has more parts of
> speech, and less nesting?

It is a myth that English has more parts of speech than Lojban's more
than a hundred.

If "cmavo" counts as one single part of speech in Lojban, then
"monosyllable" counts as one single part of speech in English too,
and English has only two parts of speech: monosyllables and
non-monosyllables.

But of course neither "cmavo" nor "monosyllable" are parts of speech
in any reasonable sense.

